This policy covers `www.eaglespancorp.com`, the website of Eagle Span
Corporation. It is written to be read, not to be skipped.

## What this site does not do

This website is a set of static pages. It does not set cookies, it does not run
analytics or advertising trackers, and it does not load fonts, maps, scripts or
images from anyone else’s servers. Nothing you do on these pages is profiled,
shared with an advertising network, or used to follow you to another site.

There is no account to create and no login, so there is nothing here that
identifies you as a returning visitor.

## What we collect when you contact us

If you send a message through the contact form, we receive what you type into
it: your name, your contact details, and whatever you tell us about the vehicle
and the work. If you call or email instead, we have whatever you tell us then.

We use those details for one thing — answering you, quoting the work and
scheduling it. We do not sell them, rent them, or pass them to anyone who is not
involved in doing the work you asked about.

## Server logs

The company that hosts this website records ordinary technical information about
requests to it, including IP addresses, in the way every web server does. Those
logs exist to keep the site running and secure. We do not use them to build a
picture of individual visitors.

## How long we keep it

Inquiries and job records are kept as long as they are useful for servicing your
vehicle and meeting our own record-keeping obligations, and no longer.

## Links to other sites

Some pages link to sites we do not run, such as our listing on Google Maps. This
policy stops at our boundary; what those sites do is described in their own.

## Children

This site is aimed at commercial vehicle operators, and we do not knowingly
collect personal information from anyone under 18.

## Your choices

If you want to know what we hold about you, want it corrected, or want it
deleted, ask us. Call {% phone /%} during {% hours /%}, or write to us
at {% address /%}.

## Changes

If this policy changes, the new version is posted here with a new effective
date.
